GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): pictures in between. HeartGold's loop runs at 30 Hz, so each
3D scene shows for two frames and everything moving on screen moves in two-frame jumps (4 pixels
at a time under a walking player). Each scene's geometry commands and objects (runs of vertices
under one clip matrix) are kept. When a scene is swapped in after one shown for two frames, its
first frame is drawn by a second geometry engine replaying it from the state it started in, every
object moved halfway back to where it was in the scene before (matched by its first vertex and
vertex count, nearest where the scene's overall motion puts it; unmatched, with that motion),
shifted in whole pixels in clip space before clipping; its second frame is the scene itself. The
picture moves every frame, at the cost of one frame: the next scene is only complete late in the
frame between. GoldLink turns it on with the steady overworld (the overworld only).

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

