+    // GoldLink (UC11): pictures in between. HeartGold's whole loop runs at 30 Hz: it draws a new
+    // 3D scene every other frame and the frame between shows the last one again, so whatever
+    // moves on screen (the world under a walking player, people, a trainer sliding in) moves in
+    // jumps of two frames. Each scene's geometry commands are kept (MidLog), and every object in
+    // it (a run of vertices under one clip matrix: a map block, a building, a person, a sprite)
+    // with where its origin lands on screen (MidObjects). When a scene is swapped in after one
+    // shown for two frames, its first frame is drawn by a second geometry engine (MidShadow)
+    // replaying it from the state it started in, every object moved on screen halfway back
+    // toward where it was in the scene before: the matching object there (the same first
+    // vertex and vertex count, nearest where the scene's overall motion puts it), or, with no
+    // match, by half the overall motion. The shift is added in clip space before clipping, so
+    // nothing is cut short at the picture's edges: the picture between is a whole scene, as the
